1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Knud immigrated to America in 1846. He signed out of the parish in Norway on May 1, 1846, along with his brothers, Thore, Erasmus, and Ole, stating that they were going to America. His brother, Thore, was married a
2 CONC nd brought his family to America along with his three brothers. They arrived in America on the ship "Vaaren". Knud and Eramus stayed in Illinois but Thore and Ole moved to Iowa.  Over the next years his widowed mother and other si
2 CONC blings also immigrated to America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their father's name was Ole Jonsen so in Norway they were named Olson (Olsen). For a short time that was the name they used in America. However, Thore adopted the surname of Sawyer and eventually the rest of his siblings adopted t
2 CONC hat name too. The name Sawyer was the English translation for Sagen, the name of the family farm in Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT Provided by Arlene Weber Mabis,
2 CONT   great great great great granddaughter
