1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/95775234/erasmus-o-sawyer
2 CONT
2 CONT His parents were Ole Jonsen and Marthe Thorsdr.   His father was born in Norway in Jan. 1792.  He died at the age of 39 on Dec. 22, 1831.  This left his mother a widow with 8 children.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The family took the last name of Sawyer because they lived in an area of Ovre Biorem where there were hills that the family had been involved in sawing as an occupation.  Thus when the family immigrated to America they used the na
2 CONC me Sawyer (one who saws wood).  A few of the family used the name Olsen for a while but eventually changed to Sawyer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT All members of the family eventually immigrated to America. Erasmus and three of his brothers, Knud, Ole, and Thore and his family, immigrated to America in May 1846.
